- Add expiry payouts, off by default with `expiry_payouts`
  In expiry payout mode the server records an owner mailbox key `M` for
  every VTXO, and the watchman pays the VTXOs of an expired tree to
  `tr(M)` instead of to the operator. The fee is the higher of 2,000 sats
  and 1% of the value of the owner in the tree, once for each owner in each
  tree. The mode is fixed when the database is created. Without it, the
  server behaves as upstream. See `docs/expiry-payouts.md`.
  [#1](https://github.com/SatoshiPortal/scuttle/pull/1)
  - `watchman.expiry_payout_max_fee_rate` caps the feerate of a payout
    transaction and of its replacements.
  - In expiry payout mode the server refuses an HTLC send or an HTLC receive
    grant that expires more than six blocks after the tip plus
    `htlc_send_expiry_delta`, and a round output with the key of round
    padding.
  - Recovery mailbox posts are stored as upstream does, for any VTXO. The
    owner mailbox that the server records when it creates a VTXO decides its
    payout.
  - `ln_receive_ark_address_hints` lets a receiver put its Ark address in
    the route hints of an invoice, so a payer on this server pays the invoice
    with an arkoor. Only a new arkoor settles the receive, and a retry of
    that arkoor is co-signed again.
  - In expiry payout mode an arkoor can create only pubkey outputs. A
    Lightning send can also create HTLC-send outputs whose expiry the
    server caps.
  - A round drops a stored delegated participation whose outputs cannot
    bind to owner mailboxes, so it does not fail each next round.
  - A retry of an arkoor that paid a receive also notifies the receiver and
    cancels the hold invoice after a server restart.
  - An invoice can be paid by arkoor only if its route hints carry an Ark
    address, even if its receive has a claim key.
  - An unregistered arkoor output to the key of round padding pays its
    sender at expiry. Only an unclaimed round padding output pays the
    operator.
